# %% [markdown]
# ## What you built, and what it cannot see
#
# You built the four checks and the gate that a biomarker report has to pass, and you measured them against an answer
# key: a finder for samples registered twice, a merge that turns them into one person, a plate balance counted by
# donor, a label shuffle that respects the clustering, and a gate that withholds the number. **What the harness cannot
# see:** a person enrolled twice, who shows up at donor-level similarity and not at copy-level (the threshold ignores
# it on purpose); a batch effect tied to something that was never recorded; a model that leaks in a way none of these
# controls shuffles; how often the batch check raises a false alarm on plates assigned at random (these balanced cohorts
# are filled in blocks, so that was not measured); and anything about a real cohort, whose plates are messier than
# these. A quiet harness is a necessary condition for a report, never a sufficient one. The capstone of this programme runs this audit before its
# biomarker shortlist.

